WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:04.980
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.380
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.960
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.220
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.360
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你带来终极的《办公室》粉丝播客。

6
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.860
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

7
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.060
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of VFF stories.
分享幕后细节，还有许多我们这对挚友的故事。

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.100
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

9
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.790
Hi there, everybody.
大家好。

10
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:27.810
Bonjour.
Bonjour（法语：你好）。

11
00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.690
Why French?
为什么说法语？

12
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.310
Why French today?
今天为什么要说法语？

13
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.110
I don't know.
我不知道。

14
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.330
I'm wearing a black and white stripy sweater.
我穿着一件黑白条纹毛衣。

15
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.650
And I just feel like if I had a red beret, I'd be very French right now.
我感觉如果我戴上一顶红色贝雷帽，我现在就会非常有法国风情。

16
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.330
You would.
确实会。

17
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.550
Well, I couldn't wear my beret and my headphones to podcaSt.
好吧，我没法既戴着贝雷帽又戴着耳机录播客。

18
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:44.170
True.
也是。

19
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:50.570
Before we get into this episode, I mean, are you dying to hear a jumping up and down update?
在进入本集内容之前，我是说，你是不是迫不及待想听听关于“蹦跳”的最新进展了？

20
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.570
Did you do your 50 jumps?
你每天都跳50下了吗？

21
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:53.990
Every day.
每天都跳。

22
00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.210
I'm doing them every day.
我每天都在坚持。

23
00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.610
My calves don't hurt anymore.
我的小腿已经不疼了。

24
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:57.750
Really?
真的吗？

25
00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:58.370
Yeah.
真的。

26
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.070
That was just the first couple of days.
那只是头几天的事。

27
00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.810
And I think there's something to this.
我觉得这确实有点门道。

28
00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.730
It's really great.
真的很棒。

29
00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:05.990
I have a question for you.
我有个问题想问你。

30
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:06.510
What?
什么？

31
00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:08.950
Are you jumping in sneakers or barefoot?
你是穿着运动鞋跳还是光脚跳？

32
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:09.430
No.
不。

33
00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.550
Not in sneakers.
不穿运动鞋。

34
00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:12.750
So here's what I do.
我是这样做的。

35
00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:13.790
I get up in the morning.
我早上起床。

36
00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.570
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

37
00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.630
I shower or get dressed.
洗个澡或者穿好衣服。

38
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:21.510
I mean, I have to put something on the ladies, some form of support before I start jumping.
我是说，在开始跳之前，我得给胸部穿点什么，提供某种支撑。

39
00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.010
Right, so they don't bounce like crazy.
对，这样它们就不会疯狂晃动了。

40
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:23.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

41
00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:23.550
Right.
没错。

42
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.030
And then I jump.
然后我就开始跳。

43
00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.930
And then I go downstairs and I get my cup of coffee and I get my morning started.
跳完我就下楼去喝杯咖啡，开启我的一天。

44
00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.190
But it's like very first thing and I'm usually, Sam, what is it?
但这真的是我做的第一件事，我通常……山姆，那是多少来着？

45
00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:36.790
How high are you jumping?
你跳得有多高？

46
00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:37.790
Not high.
不高。

47
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.050
You don't have to jump high.
你不需要跳得很高。

48
00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:39.630
Okay.
好吧。

49
00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:43.850
I'm picturing you doing like basketball style, like leaps.
我脑补了一下你像打篮球那样跳跃的样子。

50
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:44.490
Okay.
好吧。

51
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:44.890
Okay.
好的。

52
00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:50.630
No, imagine like enough for a jump rope to fit under my feet, but I'm not bending my knees.
不，想象一下，高度刚好能让跳绳从我脚下穿过，但我膝盖不弯曲。

53
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:51.990
I'm just jumping up.
我只是向上跳。

54
00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.630
And, but then I also like, I wave my arms because I just like want my arms to be part of the pumping
而且，我还喜欢挥动双臂，因为我希望我的手臂也能参与到这种律动中，

55
00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.510
of the jumping.
参与到跳跃中。

56
00:01:58.810 --> 00:01:59.190
Perfect.
完美。

57
00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.530
What day are you on?
你坚持多少天了？

58
00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:02.250
How many days?
多少天了？

59
00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.890
Maybe like 10 now or something.
大概10天了吧，或者差不多。

60
00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:05.570
I don't know.
我也不确定。

61
00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:07.410
I need to look and see when I started.
我得去查查我是什么时候开始的。

62
00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:08.630
You got to mark that down.
你得记下来。

63
00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:13.330
This is where my mind goes is that, um, cause my house is this older house, right?
我脑子里想的是，嗯，因为我的房子是那种老房子，对吧？

64
00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.050
That if our kids jump upstairs in the kitchen, we're like, what was that?
如果孩子们在楼上厨房跳，我们就会想，那是什么声音？

65
00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:18.610
Yeah.
是啊。

66
00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.830
I mean, it's so loud.
我是说，声音太大了。

67
00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:24.770
So I, I sort of picture Lee making coffee in the morning and like ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.
所以我脑补了一下李早上在楼下冲咖啡，然后听到叮、叮、叮、叮、叮的声音。

68
00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.010
They didn't mention anything.
他们什么都没提。

69
00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.410
I had to tell them I was doing the jumping.
我不得不告诉他们我在跳绳。

70
00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.910
No one said, mom, what's happening up there every morning now?
没人问过我，妈，现在每天早上楼上在干嘛？

71
00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.450
Well, you probably have better insulation than we have.
嗯，你们家的隔音可能比我们家好。

72
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:33.990
Maybe.
也许吧。

73
00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:38.390
I mean, you could drop a quarter upstairs and we're like, oh, someone dropped something.
我是说，你在楼上掉个硬币，我们都能听到，心想，哦，有人掉东西了。

74
00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:44.050
Are you still patting yourself down, Angela?
安吉拉，你还在坚持拍打自己吗？

75
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:45.710
I don't do it every day.
我不是每天都做。

76
00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.070
I don't know why that's funny to me.
我不知道为什么这让我觉得很好笑。

77
00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.850
Because it's predictable.
因为这很符合你的性格。

78
00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:55.910
The most predictable thing about me is my inconsistency with the new trend.
关于我最符合性格的事，就是我对新潮流总是三分钟热度。

79
00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.690
The only thing I'm stuck with is tennis.
我唯一坚持下来的就是打网球。

80
00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.810
Like I do tennis every week.
我每周都打网球。

81
00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:01.510
That's all I got.
我就只有这个坚持下来了。

82
00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.890
Well, listen, why don't we jump into this episode today?
好吧，听着，我们为什么不直接进入今天这集呢？

83
00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:09.210
We are going to break down the super fan of customer survey.
我们要来解析《客户调查》这一集。

84
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.110
Customer survey was season five, episode seven.
《客户调查》是第五季第七集。

85
00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:16.330
It was written by Lester Lewis and directed by Stephen Merchant.
由莱斯特·刘易斯编剧，斯蒂芬·莫昌特执导。

86
00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.350
We've got a version of Fast Facts for you, friends.
朋友们，我们为你们准备了一个特别版的“快速事实”。

87
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.050
It's called Where Are They Now?
它叫“他们现在在哪里？”

88
00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:22.890
That's what it's called.
就叫这个名字。

89
00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:23.470
Yes.
没错。

90
00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.590
Fast Fact number one is called Where Are They Now?
第一个快速事实叫“他们现在在哪里？”

91
00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:26.430
Character recap.
角色回顾。

92
00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.250
Cassie helped us with this.
卡西帮了我们不少忙。

93
00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:32.590
We thought it might be good to frame where are we now in everyone's storyline.
我们觉得梳理一下每个人的故事线进展到哪儿了会很有意义。

94
00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:40.570
So, last episode, the episode prior to customer survey, Michael and Daryl drop Holly off at Nashua.
所以，上一集，也就是《客户调查》之前的那一集，迈克尔和达里尔把霍莉送到了纳舒厄。

95
00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:48.570
This is after David Wallace caught Michael and Holly kissing at the Crime Aid fundraiser and said they can no longer work together.
这是在大卫·华莱士在“犯罪援助”募捐会上抓到迈克尔和霍莉接吻，并说他们不能再一起工作之后发生的。

96
00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:49.610
Yeah.
是啊。

97
00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.530
So, he transfers Holly.
所以，他把霍莉调走了。

98
00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.950
That was such a dick move, David Wallace.
大卫·华莱士那招真是太混蛋了。

99
00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:54.870
I agree.
我同意。

100
00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.230
How many people are hooking up in this office over the years?
这些年来，办公室里到底有多少人在搞暧昧？

101
00:03:58.710 --> 00:03:59.310
Seriously.
说真的。

102
00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.070
So many.
太多了。

103
00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.670
Angela Martin would have been transferred a long time ago.
安吉拉·马丁早该被调走了。

104
00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:03.190
I know.
我知道。

105
00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:09.650
Well, Holly doesn't think that a long-distance relationship is going to work and ends things with Michael.
嗯，霍莉觉得异地恋行不通，于是和迈克尔分手了。

106
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:10.930
It's very sad.
这太令人难过了。

107
00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:11.410
Yeah.
是啊。

108
00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.370
Pam is in New York.
帕姆在纽约。

109
00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:20.590
She is attending art school and now also working at the corporate offices of Dunder Mifflin.
她正在上艺术学校，现在也在邓德·米夫林的总公司工作。

110
00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.530
She and Jim are engaged.
她和吉姆订婚了。

111
00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:29.310
Angela Martin is engaged to Andy and Andy is very excitedly planning their wedding.
安吉拉·马丁和安迪订婚了，安迪正兴致勃勃地筹备他们的婚礼。

112
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:38.830
But Angela is also having a secret affair with Dwight that Phyllis got a glimpse of back in season four finale Goodbye, Toby.
但安吉拉还和德怀特保持着地下情，菲利斯在第四季大结局《再见，托比》中瞥见过一眼。

113
00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.730
So, there's a lot happening here.
所以，这里发生了很多事。

114
00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:43.350
Yeah.
是啊。

115
00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:52.810
And finally, Ryan is back working at Dunder Mifflin and he's sort of seeing Kelly and his reluctant, aloof dating style.
最后，瑞安回到了邓德·米夫林工作，他正和凯莉约会，带着他那种勉强又冷漠的约会风格。

116
00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:57.930
So, you guys, this episode originally aired on November 6, 2008.
所以，各位，这一集最初是在2008年11月6日播出的。

117
00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:02.050
And Jenna thought it would be fun if we did a little thing called, Where Were We?
珍娜觉得如果我们做一个叫“我们当时在哪？”的小环节会很有趣。

118
00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:02.590
Yes.
没错。

119
00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.050
Where Were We?
我们当时在哪？

120
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.650
Our fast fact, too, is called, Where Were We?
我们的速记事实环节也叫“我们当时在哪？”

121
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.750
Where Were We as Jenna and Angela?
作为珍娜和安吉拉，我们当时在哪？

122
00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.310
Angela, do you want to tell us where you were?
安吉拉，你想告诉我们你当时在哪吗？

123
00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:14.230
Yeah.
好啊。

124
00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.010
I went into my digital clutter, like you know I like to do.
我翻了翻我的数字杂物，就像你知道我喜欢做的那样。

125
00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:20.370
And I have emails for you.
我有一些邮件要分享给你们。

126
00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:20.990
Okay.
好的。

127
00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.050
That I'm going to share.
我要分享出来。

128
00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:29.210
The first one is, me and you and Jen Salata, writer, director Jen Salata, had a thread going.
第一封邮件是我们俩和编剧兼导演简·萨拉塔之间的往来邮件。

129
00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:30.070
We did?
我们有吗？

130
00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:30.650
Yeah.
有的。

131
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:38.730
The week this episode came out, in fact, Jen emailed us and said, You guys, this is what I was talking about on set.
就在这一集播出的那周，简发邮件给我们说：“伙计们，这就是我在片场提到的那个。”

132
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.010
Have you seen this?
你们看过这个吗？

133
00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.050
And it's titled, Ninja Cat.
标题是《忍者猫》。

134
00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:43.370
What?
什么？

135
00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.290
And I wrote, LOL, so awesome.
我回道：“哈哈，太棒了。”

136
00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.910
And you wrote, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.
你回道：“哈哈哈哈哈哈哈。”

137
00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.150
And I went to the video and it's now unavailable.
我点开视频，结果现在已经看不了了。

138
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:53.970
Oh, no.
噢，不。

139
00:05:53.970 --> 00:06:02.550
It was, clearly has, I mean, if titled correctly, is some sort of cat doing ninja moves?
显然，我是说，如果标题没起错的话，是不是某种猫在做忍者动作？

140
00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.190
I don't know.
我不知道。

141
00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:03.690
Ninja moves.
忍者动作。

142
00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:04.090
Okay.
好吧。

143
00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.470
But a glimpse into what we talk about on set, by the way.
顺便说一下，这让我们得以一窥我们在片场都在聊些什么。

144
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:08.270
Yes.
没错。

145
00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.790
Also this week, we got an email from Randy Cordray.
这周我们还收到了一封来自兰迪·科德雷的邮件。

146
00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.210
Aw, I just love even saying his name because I just adore him.
噢，我光是念他的名字就很开心，因为我太喜欢他了。

147
00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.270
The email is titled, Office Latest Schedule.
邮件标题是《办公室最新时间表》。

148
00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.770
And he addressed it, Hi, team office.
他称呼我们为“办公室团队，你们好”。

149
00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.630
Please see the attached schedule.
请查看附件中的时间表。

150
00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:27.730
It is now our plan to only shoot the Super Bowl two-parter in December.
我们现在的计划是只在十二月拍摄超级碗的两集特别篇。

151
00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:33.670
We will shut down production for Thanksgiving from Monday, November 17th through Friday, December 12th.
我们将从11月17日星期一到12月12日星期五暂停感恩节期间的制作工作。

152
00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:36.950
We're also going to have a table read on Wednesday, December 3rd.
我们还打算在12月3日星期三进行一次剧本围读。

153
00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.010
Oh.
哦。

154
00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:39.110
I know.
我知道。

155
00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:42.890
And then he sent us a whole schedule, which you would have loved.
然后他给我们发了一整份时间表，你肯定会喜欢的。

156
00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:46.690
And it said who was writing what episode and what director they had picked.
上面写了谁负责写哪一集，以及他们选定的导演是谁。

157
00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.190
I would love that.
我会很喜欢的。

158
00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.050
I know.
我知道。

159
00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:55.150
And then lastly, I have one where I sent you a picture of Isabel being super cute.
