而且当谎言越编越大时，他的眼里流露出那种惊奇的神情。

326
00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:11.180
But we know that Steve was doing a scripted dialogue.
但我们知道史蒂夫是在照着剧本念台词。

327
00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:11.860
Yeah.
是啊。

328
00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:14.460
But he's making it seem like Michael's discovering it.
但他让这一切看起来像是迈克尔自己想出来的。

329
00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:15.280
It's just brilliant.
真是太天才了。

330
00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:16.100
Steve is brilliant.
史蒂夫是个天才。

331
00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:17.040
We all know this.
我们都知道这一点。

332
00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:23.520
That was a big part of the Michael character that Steve had to play all the time was delivering
史蒂夫一直要扮演的迈克尔这个角色，很大一部分就是传达

333
00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.380
dialogue like that.
那样的台词。

334
00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:26.280
Yes.
是的。

335
00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:29.580
With like this sense of wonder that it's coming out of his mouth.
带着那种仿佛话是从他嘴里自然流露出来的惊奇感。

336
00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:36.240
Well, after that moment, there was one more really great couplet of dialogue that is new
嗯，在那一刻之后，还有一段非常棒的对话，对于超级粉丝来说是

337
00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:37.140
to the super fan.
新鲜的。

338
00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:42.880
Because right after Michael's speech, Andy gets very excited and he goes, big idea.
因为在迈克尔演讲之后，安迪非常兴奋，他说，有个好主意。

339
00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:45.200
We should totally do a double wedding.
我们完全可以办一场双重婚礼。

340
00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.260
You and Holly, me and Angela.
你和霍莉，我和安吉拉。

341
00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.600
And Michael goes, um, we would never do that.
迈克尔说，嗯，我们绝不会那样做。

342
00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.640
And if we did, it would be with Jim and Pam.
而且如果我们真要办，那也是和吉姆与帕姆一起。

343
00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.660
And then Jim goes, and we would never do that.
然后吉姆说，我们绝不会那样做。

344
00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.100
And Michael goes to Andy.
然后迈克尔对安迪说。

345
00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:58.140
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

346
00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:02.100
It was like, it was like multiple disses on different levels.
这就像是，就像是在不同层面上进行了多次打击。

347
00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:03.440
Yes.
是的。

348
00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.280
This got me curious about double weddings.
这让我对双重婚礼感到好奇。

349
00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:09.240
Would you ever do a double wedding?
你会办双重婚礼吗？

350
00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.260
Would I ever do a double wedding?
我会办双重婚礼吗？

351
00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:11.840
Yeah.
是啊。

352
00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:12.860
I wouldn't.
我可不会。

353
00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:16.400
No, no, no, I want the party to be my party.
不，不，不，我希望派对就是我的派对。

354
00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:17.040
Yeah.
是啊。

355
00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:18.220
I don't want to share my party.
我不想和别人共用我的派对。

356
00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:19.820
I looked into it.
我研究了一下。

357
00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:27.720
I guess only 1% of weddings are double weddings in places like the US, the UK, Canada, and Australia.
我猜在美国、英国、加拿大和澳大利亚这些地方，只有1%的婚礼是双人婚礼。

358
00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.840
There are other parts of the world where double weddings are more popular.
在世界其他地方，双人婚礼可能更受欢迎一些。

359
00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:37.740
But I ended up on some thread about double weddings.
但我最终还是翻到了一些关于双人婚礼的帖子。

360
00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.460
And there were two people who shared double wedding stories.
有两个人分享了他们的双人婚礼故事。

361
00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.800
And I thought I could share them.
我觉得我可以分享一下。

362
00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:42.840
Okay.
好吧。

363
00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.220
I mean, I guess, I mean.
我是说，我猜，我是说。

364
00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.440
I think I was on Quora.
我想我当时是在Quora上。

365
00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:46.540
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

366
00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:46.980
Quora.
Quora。

367
00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:50.140
Quora will get you a random answer.
Quora上总能给你一些随机的答案。

368
00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:51.500
You know, here's the thing.
你知道，重点是这样的。

369
00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:54.780
I don't mean to poo-poo double weddings for the 1% that have had them.
我并不是要贬低那1%举行过双人婚礼的人。

370
00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:58.380
I just, I guess maybe it saves money, right?
我只是觉得，也许这样能省钱，对吧？

371
00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:58.860
Yep.
没错。

372
00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:02.700
But you would have to really like the other people and really have the same taste.
但你必须得真心喜欢对方，而且品味要非常一致才行。

373
00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:03.280
Yes.
是的。

374
00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.820
Well, here's what one person said.
好吧，来看看其中一个人是怎么说的。

375
00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:09.160
They said, quote, I have only ever been to one double wedding.
他们说，引用一下：我只参加过一次双人婚礼。

376
00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:17.920
Two sisters whose parents had also been married in a double wedding and their father was the minister of the church.
那是两个姐妹，她们的父母当年也是通过双人婚礼结婚的，而且她们的父亲还是教堂的牧师。

377
00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:23.240
So the logistics were quite a performance, but it all went perfectly.
所以整个流程安排得像一场表演，但一切都进行得很完美。

378
00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:29.520
Secondly, this person went on to say, first, the dad escorted his eldest daughter down the aisle.
其次，这个人接着说，首先，父亲挽着大女儿走过红毯。

379
00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.940
Then he went back, escorted his younger one down the aisle.
然后他折回去，又挽着小女儿走过红毯。

380
00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.080
He didn't bother asking who gives this woman.
他没费心去问“谁把这位女士交给新郎”。

381
00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:41.920
I think he said something to the effect of, I give this woman.
我想他大概是说了类似“我把这位女士交给你”之类的话。

382
00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.180
Then he went through all the vows with one couple.
然后他为第一对新人主持了全部誓词环节。

383
00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.800
And then he did it again with the second couple.
接着又为第二对新人重复了一遍。

384
00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:54.720
So not only was it a double wedding, but the dad was the minister of the double wedding.
所以这不仅是一场双人婚礼，父亲还是这场双人婚礼的牧师。

385
00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:59.340
I mean, I feel like Michael Scott would be so delighted to be this dad.
我是说，我觉得迈克尔·斯科特一定会非常乐意当这个父亲。

386
00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:03.320
He could walk both his daughters down the aisle at the same day.
他可以在同一天挽着两个女儿走过红毯。

387
00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.500
And he gets to do all the talking.
而且所有的发言都由他来做。

388
00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.240
This is Michael Scott's dream wedding.
这就是迈克尔·斯科特的梦幻婚礼。

389
00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:13.220
I'm just asking myself if I'm the younger sister, am I annoyed?
我只是在问自己，如果我是那个妹妹，我会不会觉得烦？

390
00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:16.400
Am I like just this whole thing?
我会不会觉得这一切都很……？

391
00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:19.320
It's like, I'm the second bride to walk down the aisle.
就像是，我是第二个走红毯的新娘。

392
00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.220
I'm the second set of vows that get exchanged.
我是第二对交换誓词的人。

393
00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:26.200
Like, is everyone done kind of like crying after the first one?
大家是不是在第一对交换完誓词后，眼泪都流干了？

394
00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.620
Also, what about the bouquet toss?
还有，抛捧花环节怎么办？

395
00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:31.440
Everyone's fought it out for the older sister's bouquet.
大家已经为了抢姐姐的捧花打得不可开交了。

396
00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:35.640
And then you're like, you're like in the back one, like, you guys, I have one to throw.
然后你站在后面说，嘿，大家，我还有一个要抛呢。

397
00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:37.000
So am I, am I?
所以我，我是不是……？

398
00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:39.580
Yeah, I don't have any details on that.
是啊，我没有关于那方面的细节。

399
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.020
All right, here's my next letter.
好了，这是我的下一封信。

400
00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.060
My next Quora.
我的下一个Quora问题。

401
00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:48.780
I have been a wedding officiant for 20 years and full time for six.
我做婚礼司仪已经20年了，全职做了6年。

402
00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.200
That's literally hundreds of weddings.
那可是几百场婚礼了。

403
00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:53.660
And I've done one double wedding.
我还主持过一场双人婚礼。

404
00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:56.040
It was for two sisters.
那是为一对姐妹主持的。

405
00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.160
One was marrying a man.
其中一个要嫁给男人。

406
00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.800
The other was marrying a woman.
另一个要娶一个女人。

407
00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:10.740
So the sister who was engaged to the man held off marrying her fiance until it was legal for her sister to wed her bride.
所以那个与男人订婚的姐妹，一直等到她姐妹能合法迎娶新娘时，才和未婚夫结婚。

408
00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:16.880
And once marriage equality laws were passed, they decided to both get married in a double wedding.
婚姻平权法案通过后，她们决定一起举办双人婚礼。

409
00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:21.000
I was like, I had goosebumps by the end of this.
当时我真的起了一身鸡皮疙瘩。

410
00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:23.820
I was like, that is the sweetest thing.
我觉得这真是太暖心了。

411
00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:27.860
Yeah, that is sweet sibling, like, support and love.
没错，那是姐妹间非常暖心的支持与爱。

412
00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:29.060
That is really nice.
那真的很棒。

413
00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:29.640
That's special.
那很特别。

414
00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:30.320
Yeah.
是啊。

415
00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:30.600
I know.
我知道。

416
00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:31.680
All right.
好了。

417
00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.680
That's what I got on double weddings, everybody.
关于双人婚礼我就知道这些了，各位。

418
00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:36.120
So back to this episode.
回到这一集。

419
00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:43.680
After the credits, we have the scene where Kelly comes into Michael's office and she's carrying a stack of customer surveys.
片头字幕过后，凯莉走进迈克尔的办公室，手里拿着一叠客户调查表。

420
00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:54.140
But first she tells Michael, hey, you know, I just need you to know I'm out $100 on the bridesmaids dress that I bought for this wedding that turned out to be fake.
但她先告诉迈克尔，嘿，我得让你知道，我为那场后来被证实是假的婚礼买的伴娘礼服，让我损失了100美元。

421
00:18:54.140 --> 00:19:00.100
In the broadcast version, she sort of drops that news and then Michael says, are those the customer surveys?
在电视播出版本里，她抛出这个消息后，迈克尔就问，那是客户调查表吗？

422
00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.420
Like, the joke is that he just kind of ignores her?
笑点在于他完全无视了她？

423
00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:02.980
Yeah.
没错。

424
00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:05.860
In the superfan version, this conversation was longer.
在超级粉丝版里，这段对话更长。

425
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:11.660
And Michael expands on what it's been like for him since he lost his fake fiancee.
迈克尔还详细描述了失去假未婚妻后他的感受。

426
00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:12.920
I think we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

427
00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:19.460
So, I returned my bridesmaid dress and it was on sale, so I'm out $100.
我退了伴娘礼服，但那是打折买的，所以我亏了100美元。

428
00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.940
And I'm out of fiancee.
而且我还没了未婚妻。

429
00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:23.780
You know what that feels like?
你知道那种感觉吗？

430
00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.960
It is like hot sand that you drink.
就像你喝下去的是滚烫的沙子。

431
00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:32.820
And then you go to get a glass of water and it's just more hot sand.
然后你去接杯水，结果流出来的还是滚烫的沙子。

432
00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:35.960
And then you start thinking, why is hot sand coming out of my faucet?
接着你开始想，为什么水龙头里流出来的是滚烫的沙子？

433
00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:39.240
You want to talk to your fiancee about it, but she's gone.
你想找未婚妻聊聊，但她已经不在了。

434
00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.460
That's actually how I feel about my dress.
其实我对自己那件礼服也是这种感觉。

435
00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:51.350
I love that no matter what Michael says, Kelly's going to bring it back to her dress.
我喜欢这一点，不管迈克尔说什么，凯莉总能扯回到她的礼服上。

436
00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:56.350
But also, how did she even have time to buy a dress?
但话说回来，她哪来的时间买礼服？

437
00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:02.910
He's only had this fake fiancee for like, didn't it all fall apart all in the same scene?
他那个假未婚妻才出现多久？难道不是在同一场戏里就全崩了吗？

438
00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:03.970
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

439
00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:07.310
Do you think Kelly had bought this dress and wanted to return it?
你觉得凯莉是早就买了礼服想退货吗？

440
00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:09.650
And this is like, she's trying to get Michael to pay for it.
她这是想让迈克尔赔钱给她？

441
00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:10.870
It was like not connected.
感觉这两件事没关联。

442
00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:11.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

443
00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:13.130
Or am I missing something?
还是我漏掉了什么？

444
00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:19.310
Like, I feel like, didn't he announce he was engaged and then it all fell apart all in the same scene?
我是说，他不是刚宣布订婚，然后就在同一场戏里全崩了吗？

445
00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:22.170
And it definitely feels like it fell apart in the same day.
而且感觉确实是同一天发生的。

446
00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:22.930
Yes.
是的。

447
00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:28.910
Well, we also learned pretty quickly that Jim and Dwight didn't do well on their customer surveys.
好吧，我们很快也得知吉姆和德怀特的客户调查结果并不理想。

448
00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:34.130
And Sam, Cassie, Jenna, four minutes and 47 seconds.
还有萨姆、卡西、珍娜，4分47秒。

449
00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.170
Clacky balls.
咔哒球。

450
00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:36.750
Clacky balls catch.
咔哒球接住了。

451
00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:37.510
Yeah.
是啊。

452
00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:38.110
Yeah.
是啊。

453
00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:41.350
I just really missed a clacky ball catch.
我刚才真的没接住那个碰撞球。

454
00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:46.530
I still have the clacky balls that Cassie untangled for me in my office.
凯西帮我解开的那些碰撞球，我现在还放在办公室里呢。

455
00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:48.390
Sam, it was a gift you gave me.
萨姆，那是你送给我的礼物。

456
00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:49.390
Just want you to know.
只是想让你知道。

457
00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:50.410
Wait.
等等。

458
00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:55.690
Didn't somebody else's clacky balls get tangled and we never untangled them?
是不是还有别人的碰撞球缠在一起了，我们一直没解开？

459
00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.230
Didn't that happen?
有这回事吗？

460
00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:00.690
Are they mine?
那是我的吗？

461
00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:02.570
Are my clacky balls tangled?
我的碰撞球缠在一起了吗？

462
00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:09.090
No, mine were tangled for like almost a year because my friends, my neighbor's toddler came over and went,
不，我的缠了快一年了，因为我朋友，我邻居家的那个小孩过来，然后就……

463
00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:12.170
You guys, please hold.
各位，请稍等。

464
00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:14.190
I need to check my clacky balls.
我得去检查一下我的碰撞球。

465
00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:14.830
Holding.
等着呢。

466
00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.570
Well, are your clacky balls tangled?
好吧，你的碰撞球缠在一起了吗？

467
00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.310
You tell me.
你告诉我啊。

468
00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:20.570
Nope.
没有。

469
00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:21.270
No.
没缠。

470
00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:24.010
That's so frustrating to watch.
看着真让人抓狂。

471
00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:25.490
It's so satisfying.
看着真让人舒心。

472
00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.090
I think it's so satisfying.
我觉得这很解压。

473
00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:28.610
All right.
好吧。

474
00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:29.870
My clacky balls are fine.
我的碰撞球好好的。

475
00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:31.050
I couldn't wait.
我等不及了。

476
00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:32.110
I'm sorry, everybody.
抱歉，各位。

